+# Cancelling a Booked Visit Stays Out of Scope; Correcting One Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted. Amends [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) for NG-5 only.
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declined both changing and cancelling a visit once booked, confirmed deliberate on 2026-08-08. That ADR made a booked visit immutable and required any later narrowing to arrive as a recorded owner decision.
+
+On 2026-10-25 the owner recorded that decision at intake: "Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-5 whole.** Rejected by the owner's decision: a booked visit with a wrong date or description has no path to correction.
+2. **Drop NG-5 entirely.** Rejected: the owner kept cancellation out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+A booked visit's date and description can be corrected, under the same rules as booking (`REQ-VIS-003`). Cancelling a booked visit remains out of scope. The cancellation rationale stands: it would add lifecycle state the sample deliberately has none of.
+
+NG-4 is untouched. Deleting a visit stays out of scope.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The sample now corrects visits forward, as it already did for owners and pets.
+- A visit still carries no lifecycle state; a correction changes its date and description and nothing else.
+- Bringing cancellation into scope retires NG-5, and needs a new recorded owner decision and its own non-goal ADR.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the correction requirement the narrowing admits.
